\begin{verbatim}
uv run cfps-sim construct inspect constructs/competition/sfgfp.json
uv run cfps-sim simulate \
  --construct constructs/competition/sfgfp.json --output results/sfgfp
\end{verbatim}
Inspection supports all three targets, including an optional static amino-acid
ceiling from user-supplied pools. It excludes endogenous pools, synthesis, and
recycling. Construct-aware simulation currently accepts sfGFP only; PETase and
reteplase require separate folding and activity models. The JSON and GenBank
exchange leaves Popcorn's dependencies and existing work separate from this
project. No RBS score, codon score, or DNA design is treated as a calibrated rate.

\section{Scope and evidence}
The project separates known additions, uncertain lysate contributions, simulated
predictions, and experimental observations. No demonstration output is evidence
of a productive competition recipe. Horvath et al. provide a starting point for
dynamic lysate modeling\cite{horvath}; Chae et al. motivate modular diagnostics
of cell-free systems\cite{chae}; Nishimori et al. motivate uncertainty-driven
experiment selection\cite{nishimori}. These papers inform the planned development;
the present numerical constants have not been extracted from those studies.

\section{Installation and execution}
The project uses Python 3.11 and a committed \texttt{uv.lock}. On macOS, install
\texttt{uv} and \texttt{tectonic} with Homebrew. From the repository root:
\begin{Verbatim}
uv sync --frozen --extra bo --extra cloud --extra docs
uv run cfps-sim validate examples/recipe.json
uv run cfps-sim simulate
uv run --extra bo cfps-sim bo-demo
uv run pytest
uv run --extra docs python scripts/build_docs.py
\end{Verbatim}
The final command weaves this article and compiles it with Tectonic.
Tectonic may download TeX support files on its first run.

\section{Recipe feasibility and units}
The saved platform constraints specify a $20{,}000$ nL reaction, transfers in
$25$ nL increments, and fixed lysate, base-buffer, and DNA volumes of
$5{,}000$, $2{,}000$, and $2{,}000$ nL. These constraints must be reconfirmed
before experimental submission. Remaining supplements and water occupy
$11{,}000$ nL. For a molar stock,
\[
C_{i,\mathrm{known}}=C_{i,\mathrm{stock}}\frac{V_i}{V_{\mathrm{reaction}}}
+ C_{i,\mathrm{base,final}}.
\]
Base contributions must be supplied already diluted. Endogenous lysate pools are
excluded. Mass concentrations, activity units, mixed stocks, and volume fractions
require explicit chemical mappings before they can enter a molar model.

